{"type":"standard","title":"Xavier Becerra","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Xavier Becerra</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q1855840","titles":{"canonical":"Xavier_Becerra","normalized":"Xavier Becerra","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Xavier Becerra</span></span>"},"pageid":408979,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/HHS_Xavier_Becerra.jpg/330px-HHS_Xavier_Becerra.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":413},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/85/HHS_Xavier_Becerra.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":2400,"height":3000},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1378722462","tid":"2cc0e697-c106-11f1-8569-909293853637","timestamp":"2026-10-05T21:46:09Z","description":"American attorney and politician (born 1958)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xavier_Becerra","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xavier_Becerra?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xavier_Becerra?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Xavier_Becerra"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xavier_Becerra","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Xavier_Becerra","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xavier_Becerra?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Xavier_Becerra"}},"extract":"Xavier Becerra is an American attorney and politician who served as the 25th United States secretary of health and human services under President Joe Biden from 2021 to 2025. A member of the Democratic Party, Becerra previously served as the 33rd attorney general of California from 2017 to 2021 and as a U.S. representative from California from 1993 to 2017. He has advanced to the 2026 general election for governor of California, where he will face Republican candidate Steve Hilton.","extract_html":"<p><b>Xavier Becerra</b> is an American attorney and politician who served as the 25th United States secretary of health and human services under President Joe Biden from 2021 to 2025. A member of the Democratic Party, Becerra previously served as the 33rd attorney general of California from 2017 to 2021 and as a U.S. representative from California from 1993 to 2017. He has advanced to the 2026 general election for governor of California, where he will face Republican candidate Steve Hilton.</p>"}